    "title": "Washington Huddle OT: Daniels working his way back on the field - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Derek Forrest ,\n2 hours ago\nWASHINGTON ( DC News Now ) — On this week’s episode of Washington Huddle, Overtime , Sports Director Derek Forrest and Washington legend Santana Moss break down the Commanders’ 34–27 loss to the Atlanta Falcons.\nNow, the focus shifts west as Washington travels to face the Los Angeles Chargers. The Commanders will look to rebound and secure their third win of the season.\nWashington Huddle OT: McLaurin’s status uncertain All eyes will be on quarterback Jayden Daniels, who appears close to returning after missing time with a knee injury. A West Coast homecoming could provide the perfect stage for Daniels to make his comeback and help Washington get back on track.\nCatch Washington Huddle Friday nights at 7:30 p.m. on DCW50, and again Saturday nights at 11 p.m. on DC News Now.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to DC News Now | DC, Virginia, Maryland News, Weather, Traffic, Sports Live.",
